description:
A **generator** here is a function that returns the next value each time it is called, and `nil` when it has no more. Write helpers that take and return generators, doing no work until values are asked for:

- `range(from, to, step)`: numbers from `from` to `to` (`to` may be `nil` for endless; `step` defaults to 1 and may be negative);
- `from_list(t)`: the values of a list in order;
- `lmap(gen, fn)` and `lfilter(gen, keep)`;
- `take(gen, n)` returns a **list** of at most `n` values, and must not call `gen` more often than it needs to;
- `collect(gen)` returns a list of all values (only for generators that end).
